  levelTitle: Bridge Defender - Four Diode Rectifier
  initialPage: 0
  pages:
  - title: LEVEL 26 | ORIGINAL BENCH LAYOUT | BRIDGE
    explanation: 'The four diodes make a diamond on the workbench. Junction A is
      switch output, B is battery negative, P is load positive, N is load negative.
      Red and blue lines show separate nets; crossings do not connect unless they
      meet at a marked junction. The physical position of a diode is not its electrical
      ID: read D_BRIDGE_1..4 from Smart Slot bindings.'
    caption: PAGE 1/4 | SOURCE + SWITCH LEFT | FOUR DIODES CENTER | R + LED RIGHT
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.075, y: 0.53}
      label: 5 V
      color: {r: 0.98, g: 0.27, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: switch
      kind: 5
      position: {x: 0.22, y: 0.54}
      label: POWER SWITCH
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.78, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: d1
      kind: 3
      position: {x: 0.44, y: 0.69}
      label: D1  A >| K  ON
      color: {r: 0.3, g: 0.98, b: 0.59, a: 1}
    - id: d2
      kind: 3
      position: {x: 0.62, y: 0.69}
      label: D2  K |< A  OFF
      color: {r: 0.28, g: 0.9, b: 1, a: 1}
    - id: d3
